        "original_id": "8b2109c5-b91b-5405-9b2a-5bff3fa7863f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ralph Sampson\n- Events: 1985 NBA All-Star Game, 1986 Western Conference Finals\n- Teams: Houston Rockets, Los Angeles Lakers, Western Conference champions, NBA Finals\n\nFacts:\n- Ralph Sampson was the MVP of the 1985 NBA All-Star Game for Houston after playing 29 minutes and recording 24 points and 10 rebounds.\n- In 1986, Ralph Sampson made a buzzer-beating shot that dethroned the Los Angeles Lakers as Western Conference champions.\n- Ralph Sampson's 1986 buzzer-beater ended the Los Angeles Lakers' hopes of winning back-to-back NBA titles.\n- Ralph Sampson's 1986 buzzer-beater sent the Houston Rockets to the second NBA Finals appearance in team history.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
